<title>GERMANY: Siemens says forex boosts 9-mth sales. [CORRECTED 06:50 GMT]</title>
<headline>Siemens says forex boosts 9-mth sales. [CORRECTED 06:50 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>German electronics group Siemens AG said on Monday that around two percentage points of its 10 percent rise in sales in the period from October to June was attributable to foreign exchange rates.  </p>
<p>Siemens said sales in the first nine months of the business year that ends on September 30 rose to 71.2 billion marks (corrects from 71.2 percent) from 64.5 billion marks (corrects from 64.5 percent).</p>
</text>
